# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# local env. `.env*` rather than the three exact spellings: a backup, an export or a tool's
# scratch copy (`.env.bak`, `.env.save`) carries the same secrets as `.env` itself, and the rule
# that only names files someone thought of is the one that misses the next.
.env*
!.env-example

# tests
/tests/e2e/videos/
/tests/e2e/screenshots/
/tests/e2e/downloads/
tests_output/

# mutation testing (stryker sandbox + html report)
.stryker-tmp

# Mutation reports are generated, the incremental cache included. It is a CACHE and nothing
# automated reads it: `mutation.yml` passes `--force` to rebuild from scratch, and the PR run that
# would consume it does not exist. A local run still keeps and reuses its own copy on disk.
reports/*

# vitepress
docs/.vitepress/dist
docs/.vitepress/cache

# generic
node_modules
.DS_Store
dist
dist-e2e
dist-ssr
coverage
*.local
*.zip

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

*.tsbuildinfo
.claude

# The optional symlink that exposes tests/audit/*.md as Claude Code slash commands — see
# docs/tools/ai-auditing.md. The prompts themselves are versioned; this is one developer's
# convenience, regenerable with a single ln -s.
/.claude/commands/audit
